MENTOR: That's right. Easy Ease puts the peak in the middle: the move starts slowly, speeds up, and slows down by the same amount at the end.

I grabbed a frame at 1 s, the middle of that move, but it came back as plain purple, so I can't point out where Title is. You'll be able to see it on your screen.

**How to change the shape.** In the speed graph, each key has a handle, and how far it reaches sideways is the **influence**: how long the ease lasts.
- Easy Ease gives every key the same reach, so every move feels the same.
- A **short reach out of the key at 0.5 s** makes Title start quickly.
- A **long reach into the key at 1.5 s** makes it land softly.
- Keep the landing handle **on the bottom** of the graph. Dragging it up makes Title arrive still moving.

You can also type influence into a dialog instead of dragging. It's called Keyframe Velocity.

Your turn: shape all four pairs on Title so each one starts quickly and lands softly. That's Position 0.5–1.5 s, 1.5–3 s and 3–4.37 s, plus Scale. Say "done" when you're finished, and I'll check them.
